<Legal title="Privacy information" description="How Meet uses account details, room settings and optional browser permissions.">
  <p>Meet uses ProAppStore sign-in with GitHub or Google. Account identity, your room identifier and friend relationships support the app’s room and availability features.</p>
  <h2>Calls and browser permissions</h2>
  <p>Your browser asks before granting camera, microphone, screen-sharing or notification access. Calls use WebRTC; connection setup and in-call messages use the app’s real-time rooms. Connection setup also uses STUN services.</p>
  <h2>Notifications and contact</h2>
  <p>Push notifications are optional. If you enable them, a browser push subscription lets the app notify you about availability or someone joining your room. The contact form sends the name, email and message you enter to the platform’s enquiry service.</p>
  <h2>Platform policy</h2>
  <p>Read the <a href="https://proappstore.online/privacy">ProAppStore Privacy Policy</a> for platform account, hosting and data-handling information. For questions, use the contact form on the <a href="/">Meet home page</a>.</p>
</Legal>
